# Framework fabrication workspace

This repository declares `repository_kind: framework_source` in
`.ai-team/project-profile.yaml`. It **builds** the Governed AI Team
framework; it is **not** an installed client project.

## Your workflow here

- Normal software development: branch, code, tests, pull request.
- Do **not** run `/compile-project`, client gate cycles (G0–G4), Work Unit
  orchestration, or `scripts/ai-team/feedback.py` on this repository.
- Do **not** create `.ai-team/work-units/`, client `events/`, `evidence/`,
  or activate `.ai-team/runtime/`.
- Edit framework code under `src/`, `adapters/`, `distribution/`, and the
  installable payload (constitution, schemas, templates under
  `adapters/cursor/templates/.cursor/`).
- After changing installable payload:
  `python scripts/ai-team/sync_source_manifest.py` then
  `python scripts/ai-team/validate.py`.

Read `.cursor/rules/05-workspace-layout.mdc` for the full boundary list.

## Product sources

Human product intent lives under `docs/product/`. The Engineering
Constitution under `.ai-team/constitution/` is the **product** delivered to
installed projects — do not treat it as a runtime activation mandate on
this repository.

## Communication language

Read `.ai-team/project-profile.yaml` → `communication.language`. Reply to
the human in that language. Never translate YAML keys, enum values, file
paths, commands, or code.
